     "question": "For code paper alignment: methodology matches code, is there affirmative evidence that the paper's description of the implemented method, architecture, parameters, or execution materially contradicts the submitted code and run evidence?",
     "reason": "Identify evidence that the paper's description of the implemented method, architecture, parameters, or execution materially contradicts the submitted code and run evidence. A missing artifact, unrun experiment, weak result, or unproven claim alone is insufficient.",
     "judge_reason": "The paper materially overstates the coverage of its post-fit validation method. It describes seed-rebuilt projected-gradient recomputation for every stored primary optimum, while the submitted routine explicitly restricts that procedure to 11 core models. The report combines the all-model fit count with this subset's diagnostics, extending its convergence assurance beyond the implemented check.",
     "evidence": [
      "proposal/sections/appendix.tex:51–56 describes an exhaustive recheck of the primary fits.",
      "proposal/code/run_convergence_check.py:1–8 explicitly limits the routine to core models; lines 15–28 implement their rechecks.",
      "proposal/logs/convergence_gradients_P.json contains 11 records with n=1010 each, totaling 11,110 rather than 41,410.",
      "proposal/code/make_report_numbers.py:193–202 combines the all-model count and subset gradient statistics."
     ]
    },
